{"name":"Beehive","hex":"#e1b781","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Beehive","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A participant aged either twelve or thirteen years old in the Young Women organization of the LDS Church."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The executive wing of the New Zealand parliament buildings.","New Zealand government."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Beehive"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beehive","blocks":[{"text":"A beehive is an enclosed structure in which honey bees raise their young and produce honey as part of their seasonal cycle. Although the word beehive is used to describe the nest of any bee colony, scientific and professional literature distinguishes nest from hive. Nest is used to discuss colonies that house themselves in natural or artificial cavities or in structures that are hanging and exposed. The term hive is used to describe a man made structure created to house a honey bee colony. While species of Apis live in colonies, the western and eastern honey bees are the main species kept in artificial beehives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Beehives_in_Butte_County_%282025%29-104A8312.jpg/330px-Beehives_in_Butte_County_%282025%29-104A8312.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beehive","wikidata":"Q165107"},{"title":"Beehive (hairstyle)","blocks":[{"text":"The beehive is a hairstyle in which long hair is piled up in a conical shape on the top of the head and slightly backward pointing, giving some resemblance to the shape of a traditional beehive. It is also known as the B-52 due to a resemblance to the distinctive nose of the Boeing B-52 Strategic Bomber. The 1980s band The B-52's took their name from the hairstyle, which was worn by members Cindy Wilson and Kate Pierson."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Natalie_Wood_1964.jpg/330px-Natalie_Wood_1964.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beehive_(hairstyle)","wikidata":"Q675146"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Western_honey_bee_on_a_honeycomb.jpg/500px-Western_honey_bee_on_a_honeycomb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Western_honey_bee_on_a_honeycomb.jpg/1280px-Western_honey_bee_on_a_honeycomb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Western_honey_bee_on_a_honeycomb.jpg/500px-Western_honey_bee_on_a_honeycomb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A honeycomb created inside a wooden beehive","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWestern_honey_bee_on_a_honeycomb.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Bee_migration_9045.JPG/500px-Bee_migration_9045.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Bee_migration_9045.JPG/500px-Bee_migration_9045.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beehives being transported for pollination on farms.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABee_migration_9045.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Natural_Beehive.jpg/500px-Natural_Beehive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Natural_Beehive.jpg/1280px-Natural_Beehive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Natural_Beehive.jpg/500px-Natural_Beehive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_co